SUMMARY:Deadline: Onassis ONX: ONX Seeds 2026\, Soft Circuits for Hard Time
 s (Athens\, hybrid)
DESCRIPTION:ONX Seeds 2026 is a four-month incubation and seed funding prog
 ram run by Onassis ONX\, the Onassis Foundation's platform for art and adv
 anced technologies\, hosted in Athens in a hybrid format under the theme S
 oft Circuits for Hard Times.\n\nOrganisation: Onassis ONX (Onassis Foundat
 ion)\nLocation: Athens\, Greece\, hybrid format. Open to creators from Gre
 ece and internationally\; remote participation for non-Athens teams.\nAwar
 d: EUR 1\,000 to 5\,000 seed funding per project\, set by scope\; up to fo
 ur projects selected. Plus weekly technical\, curatorial and business ment
 oring\, online masterclasses\, studio and equipment access at Onassis Read
 y for Athens-based teams\, and presentation at ONX Exhibition Athens (17 t
 o 21 March 2027) with travel\, accommodation and artwork transport covered
  for non-Athens participants. No application fee.\nDuration: Four-month in
 cubation\, culminating in ONX Exhibition Athens\, 17 to 21 March 2027.\n\n
 More: https://opencalls.onassis.org/onx-seeds-soft-circuits-for-hard-times
 -2?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://opencalls.onassis.org/onx-seeds-soft-circuits-for-hard-times-2?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Athens\, Greece\, hybrid format. Open to creators from Greece and 
 internationally\; remote participation for non-Athens teams.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:make-a-thek-mobility-knowledge-exchange-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261104T222342Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: make-a-thek: Mobility Scheme & Knowledge Exchange Program
 me (Europe + pilot countries)
DESCRIPTION:make-a-thek\, a Horizon Europe project (grant No. 101177660) co
 ordinated by Fab Lab Barcelona at IAAC\, connects creative spaces\, public
  libraries and makers across Europe and beyond to share skills in circular
  fashion\, traditional crafts and technology. Its open call runs two track
 s.\n\nOrganisation: make-a-thek (coordinated by Fab Lab Barcelona at IAAC\
 , funded by Horizon Europe)\nLocation: Various European pilot cities (Antw
 erp\, Barcelona\, Berlin\, Budapest\, Helsinki\, Kranj\, Milan\, Opole\, R
 eykjavik\, Kyiv\, Zaporizhzhia)\; meet-ups in Barcelona (late Nov/early De
 c 2026) and Berlin (May 2027). Open to legal residents of EU member states
 \, Horizon Europe associated countries\, and the pilot countries Ghana\, S
 outh Africa\, Indonesia\, Philippines and Chile.\nAward: Mobility Scheme: 
 EUR 1\,000 flat stipend for experienced practitioners. Knowledge Exchange 
 Programme: EUR 850 flat stipend. Up to 12 participants per track annually.
  No application fee.\nDuration: Short-term mobility: single events\, works
 hops or 2-day group meet-ups (Barcelona between end of November and start 
 of December 2026\; Berlin in May 2027).\n\nMore: https://www.makeathek.eu/
 opencall?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.makeathek.eu/opencall?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Various European pilot cities (Antwerp\, Barcelona\, Berlin\, Buda
 pest\, Helsinki\, Kranj\, Milan\, Opole\, Reykjavik\, Kyiv\, Zaporizhzhia)
 \; meet-ups in Barcelona (late Nov/early Dec 2026) and Berlin (May 2027). 
 Open to legal residents of EU member states\, Horizon Europe associated co
 untries\, and the pilot countries Ghana\, South Africa\, Indonesia\, Phili
 ppines and Chile.
END:VEVENT
